# PLAN3_MEM — two clocks, no list growth, 30s hello

File: openOODA/audit/plan3_mem.oot
Wave 3 ATTACK. Read only. Own this note. Do not edit the worktree product files. Do not edit the dirty parent.

Logline: Bench takes two now_ms calls per timed phase, grows no list, and hangs closed at 30 seconds on hello.
Setup: Worktree `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-bench`. Proof files are `cli/cmd_more.oo` and `scripts/bench_smoke.oo`. Dirty parent `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda` is read-only.
Beats:
  1. Count now_ms around check and around optional run.
  2. Prove run_ooda_bench never list_push or list_new.
  3. Prove bench_smoke wraps hello in timeout 30.

## 0. Verdict

PASS

Two `now_ms(time)` calls wrap the check child. Two more wrap `--run`.
`run_ooda_bench` does not allocate or grow a list.
`scripts/bench_smoke.oo` hangs closed on hello with `timeout 30`.

## 1. Two now_ms per phase

  File: `cli/cmd_more.oo` function `run_ooda_bench`.
  Clock is `now_ms(time)` under `&TimeCap`. No `date`. No bash timer.

  Check phase (always, after the file exists):

    let t0: Int = now_ms(time);
    let cr: Result[String, String] = sys_exec(... check ...);
    let t1: Int = now_ms(time);

  Run phase (only if `--run` and check passed):

    let r0: Int = now_ms(time);
    let rr: Result[String, String] = sys_exec(... run ...);
    let r1: Int = now_ms(time);

  `grep now_ms cli/cmd_more.oo` hits four calls: t0, t1, r0, r1.
  N is `t1 - t0` or `r1 - r0`. If negative, 0.
  No third clock in either phase. No `now_ms` in the arg walk.
  No `now_ms` in `scripts/bench_smoke.oo`.

## 2. No unbounded list growth

  `run_ooda_bench` uses scalars and the inbound `args` list.

    path, do_run, i, a, oodac, src_root, prefix, t0, cr, t1, ms, r0, rr, r1, rms

  Arg walk:

    let mut i: Int = 1;
    while i < list_len(args) {
        let a: String = list_get(args, i);
        ...
        i = i + 1;
    }

  The loop is bounded by `list_len(args)`. It only reads.
  `grep` of `cli/cmd_more.oo` for `list_new` and `list_push`: no matches.
  Bench does not copy argv into a new list. It does not append
  timings. It does not grow a catalog.

  Early exits (no file, missing file) return before any clock
  and before any child. They also grow no list.

  String concat for the `sys_exec` prefix is not a list.
  Shared helpers `find_oodac` / `refuse_cli` / `find_src_root` /
  `sq` are read-only. This role did not edit them.

## 3. Hang budget 30s on hello

  File: `scripts/bench_smoke.oo`.
  Setup line: Hang budget is 30 seconds on hello.
  Drive line:

    timeout 30 ./bin/ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo

  A hang or a check longer than 30 seconds is a fail.
  That is the MEM budget. HARN matches it.

  No-file and missing-file cases have no timeout. They must
  refuse at once. `--run` is not in this smoke. emit+gcc is
  not asserted here.

